<title>FINLAND: FORECAST-HARTWALL 4-MONTH PROFIT SEEN UP.</title>
<headline>FORECAST-HARTWALL 4-MONTH PROFIT SEEN UP.</headline>
<dateline>HELSINKI 1997-05-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>A Reuters survey of analysts</p>
<p>covering Finnish equities showed a 46.5 million markka median</p>
<p>forecast for Finnish beverages maker Oy Hartwall Ab's</p>
<p>January-April profit before extraordinary items and tax.</p>
<p>		     Profit before extras, tax</p>
<p>			   (FIM million)</p>
<p>    Median		 46.5</p>
<p>    Mean		   49.9</p>
<p>    Lowest		 38</p>
<p>    Highest		64</p>
<p>(Forecasts by six analysts).</p>
<p>Hartwall's results are due on June 5 at 1000/0700 GMT.</p>
<p>In January-April 1996, Hartwall posted a profit of 21</p>
<p>million markka.</p>
<p>In February, Hartwall said its profitability would continue</p>
<p>to develop positively.</p>
<p>Contributors to the survey were Aktia Bank, Aros Securities,</p>
<p>Erik Selin, FIM Securities, Merita Securities and Opstock</p>
<p>Securities.</p>
<p>--Helsinki newsroom 358-9-680 50 292, news@reuters.fi</p>
